  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "In the notation of 21.52, let Autt (Γ) be the set of permutations τT∈ SD such\nthat (a, b) ∼ (aτ , bτ ) whenever |ab| = t for a, b ∈ D. Clearly, Aut(Γ) = t Autt (Γ).\nIs it true that for every finite simple group G we have Aut(Γ) = Aut2 (Γ) ∩ Autp (Γ),\nwhere {2, p} are the two minimal prime divisors of |G|?                  I. B. Gorshkov",
